Description: DKMS source for the Realtek RTL8821CE combo Wi-Fi/Bluetooth driver
 Realtek's out-of-tree driver for the RTL8821CE PCIe combo Wi-Fi/Bluetooth
 chip, as used in a number of consumer laptops (including HP's 25x G8
 series). The in-tree rtw88 driver only supports the Wi-Fi half of the
 chip; this driver additionally brings up Bluetooth.
 .
 This package provides the DKMS source for the 8821ce kernel module.
 Kernel headers matching the running kernel are required to build it.
 .
 This is a fork of tomaspinho/rtl8821ce, archived by its upstream
 maintainer in 2026 with no successor. See debian/copyright for why
 this package lives in non-free-firmware rather than main: the driver
 itself is GPL-2 source, but two files compile in opaque Realtek
 firmware microcode as C byte arrays with no corresponding source form,
 and that firmware is linked directly into the built module rather than
 loaded at runtime via request_firmware(), so it cannot be cleanly split
 into a separate package the way most firmware blobs are.
